From c5d11002131a55f43f5777e9ea4d679905f59727 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tangelo Dev <tangelo-dev@noreply.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 22:19:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] frd: RequestGameAuthentication and GetGameAuthenticationData

Games that go online (e.g. Mario & Sonic at the Rio 2016 Olympic Games
refreshing its online tournaments) ask the friends service to log in at
the game server login (NASC) for their game server id, then read the
result. With the HLE friends service both calls were unimplemented.

- RequestGameAuthentication (frd:u/frd:a 0x0028) does a NASC LOGIN at
  the Nintendo services server when one is set for the game server login
  (Configure > General > Network), with the game id, title id, SDK
  version and in-game name, and signals the game's event when done.
  Without that server, or when it can't be reached, the answer is 110
  (game server no longer available), which is what Nintendo's 3DS game
  servers give since they closed. Each login is logged.
- GetGameAuthenticationData (0x0029) returns the result as
  GameAuthenticationData (0x138 bytes): NASC result, HTTP status, game
  server address and port, token and server time.
- NASC form encoding (base64 with ".-*") in frd/nasc_client, with tests
  from the NintendoClients wiki examples.

